1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,080
A lottery jackpot advertised at sixteen point five million was never collected.

2
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:10,360
Say you make fifty grand a year. You'd need three hundred thirty years to earn that.

3
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:14,020
So who walks away from that kinda money? Okay, rewind.

4
00:00:14,620 --> 00:00:18,180
Meet Eddie Tipton. He worked at the Multi-State Lottery Association.

5
00:00:18,780 --> 00:00:23,080
That's one office running the computers that draw the numbers, for lotteries in many states.

6
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:28,880
A lottery computer's whole job is picking numbers nobody can guess, like a robot rolling dice.

7
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:31,840
Tap the heart if that sounds impossible to cheat.

8
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:36,300
Here's the wild part. Eddie's title was information security director.

9
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:42,240
So the guy keeping it safe is the guy who broke it? Yeah. Here's how, step by step.

10
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:46,820
Step one: he later told a court he wrote code that let him predict the winning numbers.

11
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:49,520
He knew the dice roll before anybody threw.

12
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:53,220
Step two: he said he passed those numbers to other people.

13
00:00:53,740 --> 00:00:56,640
Send this to the friend who plays every— every week.

14
00:00:57,200 --> 00:01:00,700
Step three: those people won, and shared the winnings with him.

15
00:01:01,080 --> 00:01:02,780
And this went down in five states.

16
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:07,860
Now, back to that jackpot. In twenty ten, a ticket tied to his scheme hit it.

17
00:01:08,020 --> 00:01:13,100
So guess how much of that sixteen point five million got paid. Follow, it's so good.

18
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:15,980
Nobody got a dollar. Not one.

19
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:20,120
In twenty seventeen, he pleaded guilty, meaning he admitted it in court.

20
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:23,180
He was sentenced to up to twenty-five years in prison.

21
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:26,240
So be real: is that enough for rigging the lottery?

